  "posts": [
    {
      "post_id": "93743",
      "author_handle": "monicirka",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 1 year 2 months ago",
      "body": "Hello,what kitchen blender is better for blending baby puree until completely smooth?",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-12170/#93743",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/f168a6f151586bfb8555.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-12170/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "93743"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "93785",
      "author_handle": "MollyUK",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 months 6 days ago",
      "body": "For really smooth baby purée, you want something with a strong motor and good blade design more than anything. We found a standard high-powered blender worked better than some of the “baby-specific” ones.\nAlso, adding a bit of the cooking water (or milk) while blending makes a big difference to getting that super smooth texture.\nIf you’re making small batches, a hand blender can work too — but for really silky purees, a proper jug blender usually gives better results.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-12170/#93785",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/f168a6f151586bfb8555.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-12170/",
      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "93743"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "93822",
      "author_handle": "royden3",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 2 months 3 weeks ago",
      "body": "For baby purées, I'd look for\npower and blade quality\nrather than a specific brand. A blender with at least\n800–1000W\nusually produces a much smoother texture, especially for vegetables, meat, and fruits.\nIf you're considering brands,\nNinja\n,\nVitamix\n, and\nNutriBullet\nare all excellent for getting very smooth purées. If you only make small portions, an immersion (stick) blender can also work well, but a countertop blender generally gives the smoothest results.\nWhatever you choose, adding a little breast milk, formula, water, or broth while blending can help achieve a silky consistency",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-12170/#93822",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/f168a6f151586bfb8555.html",
